mysterious and unprecedented is how  authorities have described what's  happening here since late july tons of  dead fish have been removed from the  river order which flows through poland  and germany  i have never seen such an ecological  disaster before this is probably the  worst catastrophe in the history of our  district i don't think the order has  seen anything of the scale before what's  happening is a tragedy  the cause of the mass die-off is unknown  german authorities say they found toxic  chemical substances as well as high  levels of mercury in water samples  in poland however test results weren't  consistent only trace amounts of the  poisonous metal were detected  we are probably dealing with an influx  of an external substance that must have  polluted this river  the fish seem to be drifting down river  they aren't from here they've come from  somewhere else and they have been dead  for at least a day  by thursday volunteers and anglers had  collected more than 11 tonnes of dead  fish from a 200 kilometer stretch of the  river order  environmentalists have accused  authorities of not responding quickly  enough  but poland says it has issued health  warnings  we advise residents and tourists staying  in the vicinity of the river not to  enter the water not to swim in it  the drought in europe has caused rivers  to recede biologists say low water  levels may have aggravated the  contamination and with hot dry  conditions expected to continue there  are fears more ecological disasters are  likely muhammad val al-jazeera  the royal
 

